# TensionBudget — Web Deployment & ML-Ready Cloud Architecture (Phases W1–W6)

This specification defines the migration of our verified local desktop pipeline (Phases 1–7) into a **modern, secure, multi-user cloud web application** without rewriting any digital signal processing (DSP) logic. The local Python codebase remains the authoritative source of truth and executes directly inside the browser using **Pyodide (WebAssembly)**, while an asynchronous cloud layer on **PostgreSQL** handles user authentication, session logging, and per-user ML personalization.

---

## User Review & Architectural Confirmation
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Zero DSP Rewrites (Source of Truth)**: All existing math in `preprocessing.py`, `scoring.py`, `spectral.py`, and `analytics.py` (using `numpy`/`scipy`) will run unmodified inside Pyodide WebAssembly. We only modify the hardware acquisition boundary: replacing `pyserial` with the browser's native **Web Serial API**.

> [!CAUTION]
> **Raw Signal Persistence Decision (FLAGGED)**: In accordance with your non-negotiables, **raw 500 Hz sEMG streams will NOT be uploaded to the server**. Raw samples exist strictly in temporary browser memory for real-time calculation and visualization, and vanish upon tab closure. Only discrete 10-minute feature summaries leave the user's device.

> [!NOTE]
> **Structural Auth vs. Research Data Isolation**: To comply with privacy best practices, authentication (`email`/`password_hash`) is structurally decoupled from biometric research data. Login tables NEVER touch research tables; authentication simply issues an anonymized `subject_id` (UUID), which serves as the sole link to physical metadata and ergonomic histories.

> [!TIP]
> **ML-Ready Tabular Design (Flattened Schema + Explicit Missingness)**: To guarantee type safety and native ingestion into ML engines (scikit-learn/XGBoost) without expensive JSON parsing or Parquet over-engineering, `computed_features` stores every feature as an explicit typed SQL column. Crucially, to prevent conditional MDF/MNF calculations (`NULL` during resting states) from being imputed as `0 Hz` by ML models, we enforce explicit missingness boolean indicators (`mdf_computed_left` / `right`).

