## Complete Runtime Workflow & Data Telemetry Flow

The runtime data collection operates on a clean **3-Stage Telemetry Loop**, precisely mapping physical hardware events to database table insertions:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Workstation User
    participant Browser as Browser UI & Pyodide (Wasm)
    participant API as Cloud API Server
    participant DB as PostgreSQL Database

    note over User, DB: Stage 1: Session Initiation & Personal Calibration
    User->>Browser: Click "Start Recorded Session" & do 5s Shrug Test
    Browser->>Browser: Compute personal baselines: calibration_rms_left & right
    Browser->>API: POST /session/start (subject_id, calibration values)
    API->>DB: INSERT INTO sessions (subject_id, start_time, calibration_rms) -> returns session_id

    note over User, DB: Stage 2: Real-Time Monitoring & 10-Minute Periodic Epoch Logging
    loop Real-Time Ergonomic Surveillance (Clock 1: In-Memory 50Hz)
        Browser->>Browser: Stream USB Arduinos via Web Serial & update GUI gauges
        note right of Browser: When Elapsed Time crosses 10-Min boundary (Clock 2):
        Browser->>API: POST /session/log_epoch (session_id, epoch_index, 30+ flattened features)
        API->>DB: INSERT INTO computed_features (session_id, epoch_index, composite_score, MDF, etc.)
    end

    note over User, DB: Stage 3: Teardown & Final Snapshot
    User->>Browser: Click "Stop Recording" (or close browser tab)
    Browser->>API: POST /session/end (session_id, final_epoch_data)
    API->>DB: INSERT final computed_features row & UPDATE sessions SET status = 'completed'
```

