## Database Schema Anatomy & Relational Hierarchy

Our relational database structure follows a strict **3-Tier Privacy & Longitudinal Telemetry Hierarchy**:

```mermaid
erDiagram
    auth_users {
        string email PK
        string password_hash
        uuid subject_id UK "Isolated Bridge"
    }
    subjects_metadata {
        uuid subject_id PK_FK "References auth_users"
        date birth_date
        string gender_sex "M, F, Other"
        real weight_kg
        real height_cm
    }
    sessions {
        int session_id PK
        uuid subject_id FK "References subjects_metadata"
        timestamp start_time
        timestamp end_time
        real calibration_rms_left
        real calibration_rms_right
        string status
    }
    computed_features {
        int feature_id PK
        int session_id FK "References sessions"
        int epoch_index "Window #1, #2..."
        timestamp timestamp
        real composite_score
        real short_suma_penalty
        real mdf_hz
        boolean mdf_computed
    }
    self_reports {
        int report_id PK
        int session_id FK "References sessions"
        timestamp timestamp
        int perceived_exertion_rating
    }
    alert_events {
        int alert_id PK
        int session_id FK "References sessions"
        timestamp timestamp
        string alert_type
    }

    auth_users ||--|| subjects_metadata : "issues anonymous subject_id"
    subjects_metadata ||--o{ sessions : "participates in many"
    sessions ||--o{ computed_features : "logs features every 10 mins"
    sessions ||--o{ self_reports : "collects discomfort labels"
    sessions ||--o{ alert_events : "records postural alarms"
```

### 1. Tier 1: The Privacy & Identity Firewall
- **`auth_users`**: Holds sensitive login authentication (`email`, `password_hash`). Its sole purpose is to authenticate the user and issue an anonymized `subject_id` (UUID).
- **`subjects_metadata` (De-Identified Research Vault)**: Keyed strictly by `subject_id`. Contains NO names or emails.
  - **Biological Attributes**: `birth_date` (DATE), `gender_sex` (VARCHAR), `weight_kg` (REAL - Nullable), `height_cm` (REAL - Nullable).
  - **Dynamic Age Computation**: Computed dynamically at query time via SQL: `EXTRACT(YEAR FROM AGE(birth_date))`.
  - **Dynamic BMI Computation**: When weight and height exist, Body Mass Index ($BMI = \frac{\text{weight in kg}}{(\text{height in m})^2}$) is evaluated dynamically in SQL: `ROUND(weight_kg / POWER(height_cm / 100.0, 2), 2)`.

### 2. Tier 2: The Working Session & Personal Baseline
- **`sessions`**: Created when a user begins a monitoring sitting. Linked upward to Tier 1 via `subject_id`.
  - **Calibration Storage**: Captures the exact physical baseline from their initial 5-second shoulder shrug test: `calibration_rms_left` (REAL) and `calibration_rms_right` (REAL). Storing this here ensures every historical session permanently records the baseline sensitivity that governed its scores!

### 3. Tier 3: The 10-Minute Longitudinal Feature Logs
All three analytical tables point upward to `sessions(session_id)` via Foreign Keys (`FK`), creating an unbroken chain connecting every single 10-minute snapshot back to the exact shrug calibration and physical subject profile:
- **`computed_features`**: Our flattened, wide-format tabular feature matrix. Exactly ONE row is added every 10 minutes from session start to session end!
  - Columns: `feature_id`, `session_id` (FK), `epoch_index`, `timestamp`, `elapsed_minutes`, `composite_score`, `eindex_live_left/right`, `eindex_cumulative_left/right`, `short_suma_penalty_left/right`, `total_suma_bursts_left/right`, `gap_frequency_left/right`, `apdf_10_left/right`, `apdf_50_left/right`, `apdf_90_left/right`, `asymmetry_index_ai`, `asymmetry_penalty_applied`, `mdf_hz_left/right`, `mnf_hz_left/right`, `fatigue_slope_left/right`, **`mdf_computed_left/right` (Explicit Missingness Boolean)**, and `is_fatiguing_left/right`.
- **`self_reports`**: Logs timestamped user subjective perceived exertion ratings (RPE 1–10) during the working session.
- **`alert_events`**: Captures asynchronous real-time alarms fired when posture asymmetry or muscle fatigue exceed tolerance.
- **`v_ml_training_pairs` (SQL VIEW)**: Automatically joins Tier 1 (`subjects` dynamic Age, Sex, & BMI), Tier 2 (`sessions` shrug baseline), and Tier 3 (`computed_features` + matched `self_reports`), exporting clean $X \rightarrow Y$ training DataFrames directly to `pandas.read_sql()`.

